{"message":"A $450 monthly interest credit on about $96,000 is broadly consistent with a 5.5% APY: roughly $430–$450 for a 30–31 day period, assuming your balance stayed near $96,000. Gold Savings interest compounds daily and is credited monthly, so withdrawals or lower daily balances can reduce the amount.

Your Gold Savings rate is generally 5.5% APY if you maintained at least $10,000. Eligible linked products may provide additional benefits—for example, a Gold Rewards Card can add a 0.025 percentage-point bonus, and an eligible Green checking account can boost linked Gold Savings by 0.75 percentage points. Other credit cards and checking accounts may have different benefits, and simply holding multiple products does not necessarily qualify you unless they are linked under the same customer profile.

I can review your actual savings rate, balance history, checking accounts, and cards to see whether an applicable boost is missing. For security, please provide your full name and any two of these: date of birth, email address, phone number, or mailing address."}
